Let's start by merging the square roots:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{3x^4}\cdot\sqrt{5x^2}\cdot\sqrt{10}
&=\sqrt{3x^4\cdot 5x^2\cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{150x^6}
\end{align}$

Now we remove all perfect squares from inside the square root:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{150x^6}
&=\sqrt{5^2\cdot 2\cdot 3\cdot \left(x^3\right)^2}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{5^2}\cdot\sqrt{6}\cdot\sqrt{ \left(x^3\right)^2}
\\\\
&=5\cdot \sqrt{6}\cdot x^3
\\\\
&=5x^3\sqrt{6}
\end{align}$
